[
    {
        "content": "<p>In <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/36015\">#36015</a> the question came up what is the indentation rule for the new <code>where finally</code>. I did</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">my_def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">finally</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>and <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"197836\">@Jireh Loreaux</span> remarked that</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">my_def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">finally</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>would be more in line with <code>where</code>. I have no strong feelings either way (I slightly prefer less indentation and <code>where finally</code> is probably never used with only one proof term, so you would always have four spaces at least with the second option).</p>",
        "id": 580071655,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Doll",
        "timestamp": 1773793316
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Not a strong opinion here either, but I slightly prefer 2 spaces rather than 4 here too, for similar reasons as yours.<br>\nIt would be very cool to have some guidelines so we can use this syntax more in Mathlib!</p>",
        "id": 580345710,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Carlier",
        "timestamp": 1773901401
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Isn't the answer</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">my_def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?_</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">my_def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">finally</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 580345998,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1773901627
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>to match the existing syntax of</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">my_def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">my_def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 580346027,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1773901652
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>In the standard library we use yet another style:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">my_def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"n\">b</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">my_def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n<span class=\"n\">finally</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">case</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">case</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 580346177,
        "sender_full_name": "Julia Markus Himmel",
        "timestamp": 1773901765
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Actually, the <del>pretty-printer</del> <em>formatter</em> says that <code>finally</code> should be unindented (edit: matching what Markus writes):</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">run_cmd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">logInfo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">my_def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?_</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"n\">finally</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n\n<span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>(add extra spaces wherever you like, and the output doesn't change)</p>",
        "id": 580346196,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1773901776
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"260921\">@Markus Himmel</span>, would you be in favor of changing the pretty-printer to put <code>where</code> and <code>finally</code> on the same line in the absence of auxiliary defs?</p>",
        "id": 580346259,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1773901808
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>That would match the style we use in core, but I'm not sure whether we are still in the business of fiddling with the pretty-printer given that the autoformatter is coming.</p>",
        "id": 580346484,
        "sender_full_name": "Julia Markus Himmel",
        "timestamp": 1773901919
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Is the autoformatter not planned to use the <del>pretty-printer</del> <em>formatter</em> machinery?</p>",
        "id": 580346628,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1773902037
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The pretty-printer is a transformation from expressions to syntax, while the autoformatter is a transformation from syntax to syntax. It is my understanding that they will be mostly independent.</p>",
        "id": 580346749,
        "sender_full_name": "Julia Markus Himmel",
        "timestamp": 1773902107
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Sorry, then I mispoke; in the example above, I am demonstrating the <code>Formatter</code>, which is transforming Syntax to Std.Format</p>",
        "id": 580347025,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1773902230
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Actually, I think the term pretty-printer is used inconsistently for both the delaboration and formatting steps, so I was also wrong.</p>\n<p>Either way: to my knowledge the upcoming autoformatter does not build on the existing <code>Formatter</code>/<code>Std.Format</code> infrastructure.</p>",
        "id": 580347735,
        "sender_full_name": "Julia Markus Himmel",
        "timestamp": 1773902708
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I agree that putting <code>where</code> on a new line is a lot clearer</p>",
        "id": 580407942,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1773921632
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>What I dislike about having <code>where</code> and/or <code>finally</code> entirely unindented, as in Eric's example, is that it obscures that these are auxiliary (at a glance). Usually, things that are completely unindented are top-level, and everything else is internal to a top-level declaration.</p>",
        "id": 580432219,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1773927814
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>In that case let's also include <code>termination_by</code> and <code>decreasing_by</code> in this discussion. These are usually unindented, which matches the style for <code>where</code>.</p>",
        "id": 580433093,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1773927994
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Admittedly I never use those, so maybe my opinion here is skewed.</p>",
        "id": 580446055,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1773930673
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"197836\">Jireh Loreaux</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Indentation.20for.20.60where.20finally.60/near/580432219\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>What I dislike about having <code>where</code> and/or <code>finally</code> entirely unindented is that it obscures that these are auxiliary (at a glance). Usually, things that are completely unindented are top-level, and everything else is internal to a top-level declaration.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>The reason why I think it is ok to have <code>where</code> entirely unindented is that there is no empty whitespace before it, whereas there usually is an empty whitespace between top-level declarations.</p>",
        "id": 580446669,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1773930804
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>In mathlib most of the <code>where</code>s are on the same line as the <code>def</code>, so would the convention then be that the <code>where</code> can be on a newline (and then unindented) and the <code>finally</code> has to be on a newline?</p>",
        "id": 582038426,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Doll",
        "timestamp": 1774559212
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>this is a different <code>where</code></p>",
        "id": 582038537,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1774559253
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"260921\">Markus Himmel</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Indentation.20for.20.60where.20finally.60/near/580346177\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>In the standard library we use yet another style:</p>\n<p><div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">my_def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"n\">b</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">my_def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n<span class=\"n\">finally</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">case</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">case</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div><br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Looking at this, I would say it is the same <code>where</code></p>",
        "id": 582039021,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1774559443
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>really?</p>",
        "id": 582039808,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1774559809
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm gonna check the synatax</p>",
        "id": 582039822,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1774559817
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>In any case if the same keyword has very different style convention, then that will lead most likely to a lot of confusion.</p>",
        "id": 582040082,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Doll",
        "timestamp": 1774559932
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(same as in \"it is the same english word\")</p>",
        "id": 582040240,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Doll",
        "timestamp": 1774560006
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>one of them is a <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Lean.Parser.Command.whereStructInst#doc\">docs#Lean.Parser.Command.whereStructInst</a> and the other one is a <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Lean.Parser.Term.whereDecls#doc\">docs#Lean.Parser.Term.whereDecls</a></p>",
        "id": 582040568,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1774560117
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>so they are different</p>",
        "id": 582040598,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1774560132
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Huh, isn't <code>whereStructInst</code> the <code>where</code> used for declaring a structure instance? That's different, and always comes at the end of a line.</p>",
        "id": 582040893,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1774560242
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>that's what I thought <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Indentation.20for.20.60where.20finally.60/near/582038426\">this</a> was referring to</p>",
        "id": 582041067,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1774560303
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>i like being able to write <code>where finally</code> in the same line because that's like an actual phrase in english</p>",
        "id": 582313186,
        "sender_full_name": "Violeta Hernández",
        "timestamp": 1774689414
    }
]